fact WorkItem(id: "WI-1045", description: some(value: "Retire the eval-side `RequirementArena`: a dictionary has ONE representation, and the crossing converts nothing. DESIGN: `docs/design/requirement-channel.md` §9 (rewritten 2026-08-07 in the WI-1040 session, which delivered the σ half).\n\nTODAY THERE ARE TWO. σ carries `Dictionary(sub_0 .. sub_n-1, impl: S)` — an ordinary structured value in the shape WI-1019's `TermView` announces (`dictionary_view_syms`, term_view.rs, is the one owner of both names). Eval carries a `RequirementHandle`: a refcounted slot in `RequirementArena` (`eval/requirement_arena.rs`), identity `(arena, raw)`. `eval_requirement_chain_node` converts term -> handle at the SLD->eval edge; `port_resolved_tree` converts a resolved tree -> handle for the bridge.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT A STYLE QUESTION. Two identities for one thing is a live hazard the channel doc already has to WARN about: two scratch interpreters are two arenas, so one dictionary gets two `raw()`s and every comparison must be routed through the WI-1019 view or it silently answers wrong. Retiring the arena deletes the hazard rather than documenting it, and deletes the boundary at which the two forms could disagree.\n\nMEASURED BEFORE FILING, so the shape is known and not assumed: the arena has NO SETTER (a slot is immutable after `alloc`); `stand_in_requirement` builds no cycle (a bundle over `arity` marker slots), consistent with the operation-call-model no-cycles policy; every dictionary reaching eval is ground by construction. So the thing an arena is protecting is an immutable ground acyclic `(impl symbol, ordered children)` tree — which every ordinary value carrier already holds.\n\nSCOPE: 82 `RequirementHandle` references across 8 files (`eval/{requirement_arena,eval,mod,frame,closure,value}.rs`, `kb/{term_view,typing}.rs`), 32 `Value::Requirement` readers. `Frame::requirements` and `Closure.requirements` change element type; `project(k)` becomes reading child k; `functor()` becomes reading the `impl` field; `arity()` becomes positional arity.\n\nONE SPELLING IS PART OF THE JOB, not a follow-up. The IR construction node is `anthill.reflect.Expr.construct_requirement(impl_functor = .., requirements = ..)` while the view presents `Dictionary(sub.., impl:)` — different functor, different key names for one thing. Collapse them to a single constructor; channel doc §10 item 2 already made that a condition.\n\nSTORAGE IS A SEPARATE DECISION and this ticket does not make it. \"One representation\" is shape and identity — one functor, one key set, one comparison — not which store holds it. Do NOT reach for hash-consing by reflex: CLAUDE.md's Representation note says interning is for persistent heavily-shared structure and is not implied by being matched or indexed (the discrim tree keys on structural `DiscrimKey`s, never on `TermId` identity), and a conditional provision composes over type arguments, so the distinct-dictionary family follows the carried types that actually occur — no static bound, while interned terms live for the KB's lifetime. WI-1040 emits a non-interned `Value::Entity` for exactly this reason.\n\nACCEPTANCE — each test DRIVES the capability (build a dictionary on each side, assert the value), and says at its site which case fails when the change is backed out: (a) a dictionary built by the SLD fetch and one built inside an operation call compare EQUAL with no conversion step anywhere; (b) an operation body's `var_ref(__req_*)` reads the same value the resolver bound, driven end to end; (c) a conditional provision's nested sub-dictionaries project by index identically on both sides; (d) WI-857's `NoProvider` marker slot is still refused at every dispatch read; (e) the refcount tests in `requirement_arena.rs` are DELETED, not ported — say so, since a suite that keeps testing the retired store is how a retirement half-lands. `cargo-test` green via `rustland/scripts/test.sh`."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-07T14:13:48Z"))
